## 10. THE VENDOR RE-PIN — the static gate this wave first MISSED

The first push of this branch reddened CI's `Static gates` job on exactly one member:

  [verify-gates] member vendor: exit=1 FAIL
  [verify-vendor] FAIL - asset packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js sha256 mismatch

WHY: `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js` is a SINGLE-FILE `sha256` asset in VENDOR_LOCK.json, and
rebuilding it (section 3) invalidated that fingerprint. The wave ran verify-dist-fresh/docs/comments/
manual-paths but SKIPPED `verify:vendor`, and its own evidence claimed no VENDOR_LOCK change was
needed. That claim was WRONG; this section is the correction, and the CI failure was the falsifier.

  1. reproduce        node scripts/verify-vendor.ts
                      -> FAIL - asset packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js sha256 mismatch; exit 1
  2. locked value     1d59f4c9d802848780a88635390736aeabb0d8d0da44b6fb78434e1fd2be3f8f (670950 raw bytes)
     rebuilt value    485d63766ec764111a389d151071341b1477ef92e0c6f9224189c52a11c3e37d (671838 raw bytes)
                      derived with the LOCK'S OWN single-file rule — sha256 over the RAW bytes:
                      node -e "console.log(require('crypto').createHash('sha256').update(require('fs').readFileSync('packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js')).digest('hex'))"
  3. the TOOL cannot do it: `node scripts/repin-vendor.ts` reports
        packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js: POLICY (not a failure) - single-file sha256 asset - a
        build artifact, so re-pin it by rebuilding the package that emits it, never by rewriting the lock
     and its `RepinField` type is `"fileCount" | "treeSha"` — the helper never writes `sha256`.
  4. the DOCUMENTED mechanism is a deliberate hand edit of the lock, the value derived by the gate's
     own algorithm and then PROVEN by the gate. evidence/de-omo/cores/20261008T162920Z/result.json,
     key `why_a_hand_edit` (the wave that INTRODUCED these fingerprints):
       "scripts/repin-vendor.ts has NO add mode ... The five keys below were therefore inserted by a
        scripted hand edit, with values computed by the same algorithm scripts/verify-vendor.ts uses
        (readBytes: raw unless the file has no NUL ...), then PROVEN by the gate."
     and that packet's own value line for THIS asset:
       { "asset": "packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js", "fileCount": 1, "sha256": "1d59f4c9...",
         "fingerprint": "sha256 over RAW bytes (the lock's single-file rule), 670950 bytes" }
     VENDOR_LOCK.json's `sha256` for that asset was therefore set to the rebuilt artifact's value, and
     the artifact + the re-pin ride in the SAME commit (AGENTS.md §9's pairing rule).
  5. proof            node scripts/verify-vendor.ts
                      -> PASS - 7 shipped asset(s) fingerprinted, upstream identity not checked; exit 0

